framework ArchitectureDecisionRecord:
  requires problem and decision
  requires premise and evidence
  warns pending

domain ADR0015:
  description "LLMTHINK canonical ADRs with advisory sealgraph projection"

problem P1:
  |
    Markdown-only ADRs mix causal decision structure, human explanation, and
    approval state in one document. That makes unsupported conclusions and
    ambiguous status transitions difficult to detect before implementation.

premise DRIVER_CAUSALITY:
  |
    The authoritative record must expose which observations, constraints, and
    prior decisions support each selected direction.

premise DRIVER_READABILITY:
  |
    Reviewers still need a concise human-readable ADR without requiring them to
    read or operate the LLMTHINK DSL.

premise DRIVER_AUTHORITY:
  |
    An agent may draft and audit an ADR, but only the named decision owner may
    change the exact proposed decision to Accepted.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Considered options are: keep Markdown as the only authoritative artifact;
    make Markdown and LLMTHINK independently authoritative; or make LLMTHINK
    authoritative with Markdown as a human-readable projection. Independent
    dual authority is rejected because disagreement would leave no deterministic
    source of truth.

evidence E1:
  |
    The locally installed LLMTHINK help identifies .think as the standard file
    extension and .dsl as a compatibility alias, and supports explicit
    decision based_on relationships plus audit.

evidence E2:
  |
    On 2026-08-14, the repository owner requested that ADRs be written with
    LLMTHINK and that sealgraph be used experimentally only as a secondary
    check because breaking changes remain possible.

decision D1 based_on P1, DRIVER_CAUSALITY, DRIVER_READABILITY, OPTIONS, E1, E2:
  |
    For ADR-0015 and later ADRs, the same-basename .think file is the
    authoritative decision and causal record. The .md file is a human-readable
    projection. If the two disagree, the .think file controls and the projection
    must be corrected. ADR-0001 through ADR-0014 retain their existing Markdown
    authority unless a later accepted migration ADR replaces it.
  annotation caveat:
    "Accepted through OWNER_ACCEPTANCE on 2026-08-14."

decision D2 based_on D1, DRIVER_AUTHORITY, E2:
  |
    A new ADR begins as Proposed. Accepted requires evidence in the authoritative
    .think file that the named decision owner explicitly approved the exact ADR
    identity and decision revision. A request to draft, inspect, or continue work
    is not acceptance. The drafting agent must not create its own approval
    evidence or infer acceptance from an implementation instruction.
  annotation caveat:
    "Accepted through OWNER_ACCEPTANCE on 2026-08-14."

problem P2:
  |
    sealgraph can independently project dependency edges and reveal stale or
    inconsistent provenance, but its 0.1.0-dev CLI and storage contract are under
    active development and may change incompatibly.

decision D3 based_on P2, D1, E2:
  |
    Use sealgraph only as an experimental, reproducible secondary projection of
    selected LLMTHINK based_on and artifact dependencies. Run it in isolated
    disposable storage. Its findings may trigger investigation, but sealgraph
    output must never become the ADR source of truth, rewrite the .think file,
    supply owner approval, or independently accept, reject, authorize, or block
    an ADR. Missing or incompatible sealgraph is reported as advisory and is not
    a required CI or release gate while this decision remains in effect.
    Persisted sealgraph storage and reports are disposable caches. Every
    projection must be reconstructable from the authoritative .think file and
    its referenced source artifacts without reading earlier sealgraph storage.
    When a new sealgraph version cannot read old storage, discard that cache and
    rebuild only after adapting the advisory projection to the new CLI contract.
  annotation caveat:
    "Accepted through OWNER_ACCEPTANCE on 2026-08-14."

problem P3:
  |
    Existing ADR status labels do not consistently include durable evidence of
    the owner's exact acceptance instruction.

decision D4 based_on P3, D2:
  |
    Do not rewrite historical ADR decisions or statuses during this migration.
    Inventory their acceptance provenance separately. When provenance is absent
    or ambiguous, record it as unknown and obtain explicit owner confirmation
    before relying on that ADR alone to authorize new implementation.
  annotation caveat:
    "Accepted through OWNER_ACCEPTANCE on 2026-08-14."

evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    On 2026-08-14, the product owner explicitly stated: "OK、D1～D4は承認します。
    ただし注意点は、 sealgraph はあくまでも参考で、新バージョンでは「読み出せない」
    破壊的変更が起きうる（今まさにその更新を行ってる）ので注意して、原本から復元可能に
    しておいてください。" The accepted scope is D1 through D4 with the
    rebuildability condition incorporated into D3.

decision ACCEPTANCE based_on D1, D2, D3, D4, OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  |
    ADR-0015 is Accepted. D1 through D4 authorize the bounded workflow and
    migration changes described by this ADR, including a reconstruct-only,
    non-authoritative sealgraph adapter.
  annotation rationale:
    "The named decision owner explicitly approved D1 through D4 and supplied the D3 compatibility condition."
